# Guest Details

Each guest has a detailed profile containing their personal information, RSVP status, and communication history. This guide explains how to access and manage guest details.

## Opening Guest Details

To view a guest's details:

1. Navigate to your event's **Guests** tab
2. Click on any guest row in the table

The guest detail panel will slide in from the right side. On mobile devices, this opens as a full-screen page with swipe-back gesture support.

## Guest Information

The guest detail panel displays:

### Personal Details

- **Name** - First name, last name, and title (Mr., Mrs., Dr., etc.)
- **Email** - Primary contact email address
- **Phone** - Contact phone number
- **Position** - Job title or role
- **Organization/Entity** - Company or organization name

### Event-Specific Information

- **Category** - Guest's assigned category (e.g., AAA, VIP, Standard)
- **RSVP Status** - Current response status (Pending, Confirmed, Declined, Maybe)
- **Dietary Requirements** - Any food preferences or restrictions
- **Accessibility Needs** - Special accommodation requirements

## Guest Actions

From the guest detail panel, you can perform several actions:

### Edit Guest Information

Click the **Edit** button to modify any guest details. Changes are saved automatically when you close the edit mode.

### Copy RSVP Link

Each guest has a unique, personalized RSVP link. Click **Copy RSVP Link** to copy it to your clipboard for sharing via email or messaging.

### Regenerate RSVP Token

If you need to invalidate a guest's existing RSVP link and create a new one:

1. Click the **Edit** button to enter edit mode
2. Scroll to the bottom of the form
3. Click **Regenerate RSVP Token**
4. Confirm the action

{% callout type="warning" %}
Regenerating a token will invalidate any previously shared RSVP links for this guest.
{% /callout %}

### Change Status

Manually update a guest's RSVP status:

1. Click on the current status badge
2. Select the new status from the dropdown
3. The change is saved immediately

### Change Category

Reassign a guest to a different category:

1. Click on the current category badge
2. Select the new category from the dropdown

### Delete Guest

To remove a guest from the event:

1. Click the actions menu (three dots)
2. Select **Delete**
3. Confirm the deletion

{% callout type="error" %}
Deleting a guest is permanent and cannot be undone. All associated RSVP data will be lost.
{% /callout %}

## Closing the Panel

Click the **X** button or click outside the panel to close it. On mobile, you can also swipe right to close.
